    {
      "id": "claim_4bc9bb71974e492f881412d3052d060e",
      "statement": "Bare `@proxy` is deliberately excluded from the annotation gate because it is an INVALID schema: `proxy rules` reports such an item as `omit` (withheld entirely) and `varlock load` fails validation outright, so `_varlock_resolve` already returns None and the launch reports the failure. Excluding it from the gate costs no warning that the resolution path is not already making more loudly. The matched annotation shapes are measured against varlock 1.17.0.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/harnessed/launchenv.py#L78-L87",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8bc8ed7447f7bdb5570d8e802ee40c58df0c17c98f2b177579ab774c3e0ae751:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_868d33d6e8714497aafb80db8d3926b6",
      "statement": "`_schema_declares_proxy`'s two documented limits both err toward a missing warning rather than a false one: it reads the entry schema only, so a `@proxy` living exclusively in an imported fragment is missed and must be revisited when recipe `env.schema` fragments land (issue #388 Phase 1); and prose that happens to quote a full annotation (e.g. `use @proxy=passthrough for these`) still matches, which is unavoidable without parsing and costs one spurious subprocess rather than a wrong claim about anybody's secrets. An unreadable or absent schema returns False with no subprocess.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/harnessed/launchenv.py#L281-L293",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:026f9ec9d5126418969578977d43b3ff1ca56d2048434482d94ffa86b672ea36:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8232b7a69517450d9b21d8c9aa6d108e",
      "statement": "`_varlock_proxy_modes` is the only source of per-item proxy mode — `varlock load --format json-full` reports `isSensitive` and the schema-wide egress setting but nothing per item — and `varlock proxy rules` prints for humans with no `--format json`, so it parses display text that will drift. It refuses to guess: both the `Rules (N)` and `Secrets (N)` headers must have been seen and the number of parsed secret lines must equal the `Secrets (N)` count, or it returns None and the caller reports that the output could not be classified. A guardrail that quietly stops guarding is the failure mode the source explicitly refuses to repeat, citing the open bug #429.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/harnessed/launchenv.py#L296-L345",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:42f4968853490db481c74b171d8e17a8b65f1ea28610c0858a4e8af3992ea27c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_68d90b2c397a4d85a71c5fa696cf3a7d",
      "statement": "`_varlock_proxy_modes` runs `varlock proxy rules` as a subprocess under the same `_VARLOCK_TIMEOUT` (60s) deadline as `varlock load`, because the command resolves values and can block on a secrets-manager unlock. A `TimeoutExpired`, an `OSError`, or a non-zero exit all degrade to a None result rather than failing or blocking the launch.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/harnessed/launchenv.py#L313-L321",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8316e6013206c41425502e443e14c23b8f1872e18dae89ec5ae34ad28be2548d:"
