    {
      "id": "claim_e14f180f21bf402db6797423a745966e",
      "statement": "Two pieces of module state make the four call sites cheap and consistent for the lifetime of one CLI process, which is exactly one launch: `_PROXY_WARNED` records dirs already warned so the warning prints once per schema dir per launch, and `_PROXY_MODES_CACHE` memoizes the per-dir `{KEY: mode}` result (None included) with the same one-process/one-launch rationale as `_VARLOCK_CACHE` — `proxy rules` is a subprocess, both launch paths ask the same dirs, and one launch must see a consistent classification. Both are cleared by `_varlock_cache_clear()`.",
